# Interview Gold Question 🎤

## Why Not Modulo Hashing?

Because adding/removing nodes causes massive rehashing.

---

## Why Consistent Hashing?

Minimizes data movement.

---

## Why Virtual Nodes?

Better load balancing.

---

## Why Clockwise Lookup?

Simple deterministic ownership.

---

## What Happens On Node Failure?

Keys shift to next clockwise node.

---

## Biggest Benefit?

Scalability with minimal data migration.

---

# Complexity Intuition

Finding node:

```
Binary Search

O(log N)
```

if ring sorted.

---

Data Movement

Modulo Hashing:

```
≈ Almost all keys
```

---

Consistent Hashing:

```
≈ Only neighboring range
```

Huge difference.

---

# Cheat Sheet 📌

```
Problem
=======
Modulo hashing causes huge rehashing.

Formula
=======
hash(key)%N

Issue
=====
N changes => almost all keys move.

Solution
========
Consistent Hashing

Idea
====
Place nodes and keys on ring.

Rule
====
Move clockwise.
First node owns key.

Node Add
========
Only nearby keys move.

Node Remove
===========
Keys move to next node.

Virtual Nodes
=============
Multiple ring positions
for same physical node.

Benefits
========
✔ Scalable
✔ Minimal migration
✔ Better balancing
✔ Easy node addition/removal

Used In
=======
Cassandra
Dynamo
Riak
Memcached

Alternatives
============
Fixed Partitions
Dynamic Partitioning
```

